# KiCad CLI scratch / DRC-ERC report artifacts (regenerated on demand)
# Ignore everything in .tmpwork/ EXCEPT the pinned pins.json snapshot that the
# board generators load at import via std_pins() -- without it a fresh clone
# cannot regenerate the checked-in boards. Rebuild (or upgrade to current KiCad
# libs) with `python3 tools/build_pins_json.py`; see its docstring for the
# pinned-vs-builder distinction (USB_C_Receptacle pin count differs across
# KiCad versions). Using .tmpwork/* (not .tmpwork/) so the negation can reach
# the file -- a trailing-slash directory exclude blocks all re-includes.
.tmpwork/*
!.tmpwork/pins.json
hardware/pcb/*erc*.txt
hardware/pcb/*drc*.txt
hardware/pcb/*erc*.json
hardware/pcb/*drc*.json
hardware/pcb/qssc.json
hardware/pcb/t*.kicad_sch
/tools/bin/

# FreeRouting (Specctra DSN/SES) + freeroute.py build artifacts -- derived from
# the committed .kicad_pcb on demand by `python3 tools/freeroute.py`. The
# freerouting.jar binary itself lives in /tools/bin/ (ignored above); see
# tools/freeroute.py for how to obtain the pinned 2.1.0 jar.
hardware/pcb/*.dsn
hardware/pcb/*.ses
hardware/pcb/*.freeroute.log
hardware/pcb/*.freeroute.stdout
hardware/pcb/*.freeroute.drc.json

# KiCad live-edit lock files
hardware/pcb/~*.lck
